# Request collection for the service, in the plain-text .http format that
# editors such as VS Code (REST Client) and JetBrains IDEs run.
# Start the service first (make start), then send a request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Liveness probe: 200 with the body "pong"
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping

### Health check: 204 without a body, or a 500 problem document that lists the failing dependencies
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### List the resources, newest first; page starts at 1, itemsPerPage is 1 to 100 (a bare JSON array)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/example_api_resources?page=1&itemsPerPage=30

### Create a resource: 201 with the resource and a location header; 422 when validation fails
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/example_api_resources
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example name",
  "description": "Example description"
}

### Retrieve one resource by identifier: 200, 400 for an invalid identifier, 404 when it does not exist
# Replace the identifier with the id returned by the create request.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/example_api_resources/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe

### GraphQL query: one page of resources (page and itemsPerPage have defaults)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($page: Int!, $itemsPerPage: Int!) { exampleApiResources(page: $page, itemsPerPage: $itemsPerPage) { id name description } }",
  "variables": { "page": 1, "itemsPerPage": 30 }
}

### GraphQL query: one resource by id (null when it does not exist)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($id: ID!) { exampleApiResource(id: $id) { id name description } }",
  "variables": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe" }
}

### GraphQL mutation: create a resource
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: CreateExampleApiResourceInput!) { createExampleApiResource(input: $input) { id name description } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "name": "Example name", "description": "Example description" } }
}
